==French==
===Article===
{{infl|fr|article|head=[[de]] [[la]]|g=f|masculine|du|plural|des}}

# [[some|Some]]; ''the feminine partitive article''.
#: ''Voudriez-vous '''de la''' confiture ?'' — Would you like '''some''' jam?
#: ''J'ai mangé '''de la''' tarte ?'' — I ate '''some''' pie.

====Usage notes====
* While English does have the partitive determiner {{term|some}}, the French article {{term||de la}} frequently translates to nothing at all in English; for example, the above example « J'ai mangé '''de la''' tarte ? » could also be translated simply as “I ate pie.”
* Like the definite article {{term|la}} (from which it derives), the partitive article {{term||de la}} undergoes elision, becoming {{term|de l'-|de l’-}} before most words that start with vowel sounds.

